{"name":"Rock Lobster","hex":"#f00b52","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rock lobster","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A crustacean of the family Palinuridae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rock_lobster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rock Lobster","blocks":[{"text":"\"Rock Lobster\" is a song by American band the B-52's, written by their singer Fred Schneider and guitarist Ricky Wilson. It was recorded and released as a single twice, first by DB Records as their debut release in April 1978, and re-recorded the following year for the band's self-titled debut album on Warner Bros. (US) and Island Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/db/Rock_Lobster_-_B-52s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_Lobster"},{"title":"Spiny lobster","blocks":[{"text":"Spiny lobsters, also known as langustas, langoustes, or rock lobsters are marine decapod crustaceans belonging to the family Palinuridae. Spiny lobsters are also, especially in Australia, New Zealand, Ireland, South Africa, and the Bahamas, called crayfish, sea crayfish, or crawfish, terms which elsewhere are reserved for freshwater crayfish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/California_spiny_lobster.JPG/330px-California_spiny_lobster.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spiny_lobster"},{"title":"Lobster","blocks":[{"text":"Lobsters are malacostracan decapod crustaceans of the family Nephropidae or its synonym Homaridae. They have long bodies with muscular tails and live in crevices or burrows on the sea floor. Three of their five pairs of legs have claws, including the first pair, which are usually much larger than the others. Highly prized as seafood, lobsters are economically important and are often one of the most profitable commodities in the coastal areas they populate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/KreeftbijDenOsse.jpg/330px-KreeftbijDenOsse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lobster"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Jasus_edwardsii.jpg/500px-Jasus_edwardsii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Jasus_edwardsii.jpg/1280px-Jasus_edwardsii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Jasus_edwardsii.jpg/500px-Jasus_edwardsii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jasus edwardsii","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJasus_edwardsii.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Pesca_de_Langosta_con_Nasa_en_Los_Roques%2C_Venezuela.jpg/500px-Pesca_de_Langosta_con_Nasa_en_Los_Roques%2C_Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Pesca_de_Langosta_con_Nasa_en_Los_Roques%2C_Venezuela.jpg/1280px-Pesca_de_Langosta_con_Nasa_en_Los_Roques%2C_Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Pesca_de_Langosta_con_Nasa_en_Los_Roques%2C_Venezuela.jpg/500px-Pesca_de_Langosta_con_Nasa_en_Los_Roques%2C_Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fishing for Panulirus argus in Venezuela","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APesca_de_Langosta_con_Nasa_en_Los_Roques%2C_Venezuela.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Lobsters_awaiting_purchase%2C_Trenton%2C_ME_IMG_2477.JPG/500px-Lobsters_awaiting_purchase%2C_Trenton%2C_